# Backend

- Single app: `backend/api`. Put new models, serializers, views, urls, and admin there
- New data: model → migration → register in `admin.py`
- Public reads follow existing `*ListAPIView` / `AllowAny` patterns unless the task adds auth
- `Member` is the exec org chart. Do not add paid-membership fields to it
- `Registration` is anonymous RSVP with unique `(event, email)`. Extend carefully; keep public RSVP working
- Never persist student number, SIN, passport, or full payment card data
- No Django email backend exists yet; do not assume server-side mail is configured
- Settings and secrets come from environment variables (`backend/.env.example`)
